      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T17:27:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this mean that `dfp_consume_attention` may read uninitialized memory? (Do DP Attentions always have 1 VDO?)",
      "revId": "3d12473948d545c387857d81cdad340c5322dfd4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b20b5ad_002b9bd1",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 518,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-25T05:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "DP Attentions are always defined to have 1 VDO.  So it\u0027s fine for DP, but arguably the generic \"dfp_consume_attention\" should take a length to know whether there\u0027s a valid VDO.\n\nSince that function checks that we\u0027ve entered a mode before consuming the Attention, we\u0027re generally safe from mishaps here.  But I suppose that can be expounded upon via the codified commentary",
      "parentUuid": "504a5779_a2cf2e15",
      "revId": "3d12473948d545c387857d81cdad340c5322dfd4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
